st` passed at `1.0000`, and a fresh quick `run_benchmark` reached `11849.04 QPS` at `1.0000` recall. Current expectation is still low-`12k` quick on the scored cache path and mid-`5k` exact on ANN.\n\nNext best move is a stronger subcluster or residual shortlist signal, likely cluster-local codebooks or another routing stage that changes the recall curve itself. Local-centroid routing precision alone and transport read-path micro-tuning are both parked.",
